 "Expect to be told you are drying washing indoors and not opening windows. Sometimes lifestyle is genuinely part of it. But mould is also caused by cold surfaces, missing or broken extract fans, windows that will not open, poor insulation and heating too expensive to run — and those sit on the landlord's side of the line, because they are part of whether the home is fit.": "",
 "Free tool for renters in Wales. Work out what your damp or mould is, learn your landlord's duties, and write a dated report to send them.": "",
 "Housing is devolved, so Britain now has three different systems. England's Awaab's Law came into force in October 2025 and applies to social landlords, giving them 10 working days to investigate and 5 to make the home safe. Scotland's version starts on 6 October 2026 and is the only one of the three that covers private landlords too. Wales has fixed WHQS timescales for social landlords since April 2026, and the continuous fitness duty for everyone else.": "",
 "I reported this by phone on 3 March and again on 20 April. My daughter has asthma. The extractor fan in the bathroom has never worked.": "",
 "If the extractor fan in your bathroom or kitchen does not work, say so explicitly in writing. It is a concrete defect, it is cheap to fix, and it undercuts the lifestyle argument immediately.": "",
